## Control {{controlId}}: Employ the Principle of Least Functionality by Configuring Systems to Provide Only Essential Capabilities

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization employs least functionality within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through device configuration profiles restricting system capabilities and application protection policies limiting software execution, managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
**Endpoint Least Functionality:**
{{deviceConfigurationsCount}} device configuration profiles restrict managed endpoints to essential capabilities:
{{#if configurations}}
{{#each configurations}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{platformType}}){{#if description}} — {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Configuration profiles disable unnecessary services, protocols, and features:
- Unnecessary Windows features and optional components disabled
- USB storage and removable media restricted per data protection policies
- Browser extensions limited to approved list
- PowerShell constrained language mode enforced for standard users
{{else}}
Device configuration profiles for least functionality have not been established.
{{/if}}

{{#if appProtectionsActive}}
**Application Restrictions:**
{{appProtectionsCount}} application protection policies restrict app capabilities to essential functions, preventing data leakage through unauthorized application features.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine device configuration profiles, disabled service lists, application restriction policies, and endpoint security baselines.

